  "tagline": "In-process columnar SQL database: the SQLite of analytics, running inside your app or notebook.",
  "description": "DuckDB is an embedded analytical database that runs inside the host process (Python, R, Node, Java, the CLI or the browser via WASM) with no server to manage. Its vectorized, parallel engine queries Parquet, CSV, JSON, Iceberg and Delta files directly, plus its own single-file database format, and it routinely handles hundreds of gigabytes on a laptop. Official extensions add spatial, full-text, vector search and lakehouse formats including DuckLake. It has become the default local analytics and data-engineering tool; it is not a multi-user server and scales up, not out.",
